<title>SOUTH AFRICA: LANGEBERG LIFTS YR SHR, EXPECTS RAND BOOST.</title>
<headline>LANGEBERG LIFTS YR SHR, EXPECTS RAND BOOST.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   49.7	  vs 37.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 16.0	  vs 12.5 </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   80.1	  vs 54.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   107.1	 vs 94.3</p>
<p>    Tax			 27.3	  vs 29.9</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   2.9	   vs 4.7 received</p>
<p>    Turnover		  959.9	 vs 862.0</p>
<p>Div payable January 10</p>
<p>on register December 6</p>
<p>Full name: Langeberg Holdings Ltd </p>
<p>NOTE - Canning group Langeborg said international market</p>
<p>conditions were expected to weaken slightly but this should be</p>
<p>more than offset by improved profits in rand terms. </p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
